# i915.mapfile -- scope every symbol of the linked i915 module local except the
# module interface krtld resolves by name.
#
# WHY: iwm and i915 both carry an OpenBSD-kernel-API compat layer, and both
# define the SAME global names (tsleep, wakeup, bus_dmamap_*, timeout_*,
# task_*, pci_conf_read, loadfirmware, systq, ...). krtld binds a loading
# module's non-local symbols to an existing definition (uts/common/krtld/
# kobj.c do_symbols -> kobj_lookup_all), so whichever of the two loads second
# gets its compat references cross-wired into the first module's copies -- two
# unproven drivers sharing one driver's internals. Measured on dixi: with iwm
# loaded, 33 i915 references resolved into iwm's address range.
#
# The fix is to export nothing from either module except what the kernel loader
# actually looks up by name. krtld/modctl resolve exactly:
#   _init  (modctl.c mod_init -> kobj_lookup(mp, "_init"))
#   _fini
#   _info  (modctl.c -> kobj_lookup(mp, "_info"))
#   _depends_on (krtld kobj.c depends_on -> lookup_one(mp, "_depends_on"));
#             i915 defines `char _depends_on[] = "misc/gfx_private"`, so krtld
#             loads gfx_private before i915. This symbol MUST stay global.
# Everything else -- modlinkage, dev_ops, every compat global -- is referenced
# only from inside the module (via mod_install) and is resolved at link time by
# the module's own symbol table, so it can be local.
#
# Pattern and syntax copied from the gate's own kernel-module mapfiles
# (uts/common/zmod/mapfile and uts/common/ctf/mapfile): a version-2 mapfile
# with SYMBOL_SCOPE { global: <interface>; local: *; }, applied at the
# `ld -r` step together with -Breduce so the reduction takes effect in a
# relocatable object.
#
# NOTE: new solnix build glue, not derived from any GPL source.

$mapfile_version 2

SYMBOL_SCOPE {
	global:
		_init;
		_fini;
		_info;
		_depends_on;
	local:
		*;
};
